# L §4.4 (tally 2.3, #247; G3 under §12a: `window(e1, e2)` stays an expression): a window in a move's own
# `on` is a hole day named by its movement (`unknown day: pay`); one computed in a def's rule sits in that
# cell (`unknown day: gd`), and a pin of the cell answers it. A guard: the same bytes before.
=== m.tally
model onw
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date
input lo: date
input hi: date
input k: int
def gd: date
  rule base = window(wd, add_days(wd, k))
move pay: transfers
  on window(lo, hi)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move pay2: transfers
  on gd
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "c"
  wd = 2026-06-01 "c"
  lo = 2026-05-04 "c"
  hi = 2026-05-06 "c"
  k = 2 "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
ask b2_p: bal(konto, 2026-06-30) with gd = 2026-06-02
ask g: gd
=== expect
b: ?"date within window(2026-05-04, 2026-05-06) not precise enough for the day of pay" (pay) ?"date within window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-03) not precise enough for the day of pay2" (gd)
  unknown day: gd
  unknown day: pay
  cut 2026-04-20
b2_p: ?"date within window(2026-05-04, 2026-05-06) not precise enough for the day of pay" (pay)
  pinned: gd = 2026-06-02
  unknown day: pay
  cut 2026-04-20
g: window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-03)
  cut 2026-04-20
